OL,3,GNEWSAQuarter of South East             
OL,4,Ahome-schooled children have SEND       
OL,6,FAt least a quarter of children who are 
OL,7,Fhome-educated in Kent, Surrey and      
OL,8,FSussex have a special educational need 
OL,9,For disability (SEND), data obtained by 
OL,10,Fthe BBC shows.                         
OL,12,FFamilies have told BBC South East they 
OL,13,Fdecided to home-educate their children 
OL,14,Fafter feeling it was "the only thing   
OL,15,Fleft to do" and received little support
OL,16,Ffrom schools and local authorities.    
OL,18,FAn education expert said school budgets
OL,19,Fmade it difficult to provide specialist
OL,20,Fprovision.                             
